      ":question/problem": "$\\displaystyle\\int \\left(3-x^{3}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x=$\n\n{{selection}}",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Applying the sum rule, we compute the sum of the integrals of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\left(3-x^{3}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x &= \\int \\left(3-x^{3}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\ &= 3\\int 1\\,\\mathrm{d}x-\\int x^{3}\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\ &= 3\\frac{x^{0+1}}{(0+1)}-\\frac{x^{3+1}}{(3+1)}+C \\\\ &= 3x-\\frac{x^{4}}{4}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$",
